{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-127616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),\\sqrt{3},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2),0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),\\sqrt{3},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2),0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2) & \\sqrt{3} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2) & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2) & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2)-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡(t+2)-{cos}^{2}⁡(t+2)),0-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),1,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-127616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),1,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),1,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+2),1,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+2)⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1),0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1),0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1) & 1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1) & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1)\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1) \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1) & 1 \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1) & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1)-0,-({sin}^{2}⁡(2t-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2t-1)),0+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),-1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),-1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),-2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),1,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),0,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-1),-1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,4⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,4⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 4 \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 4 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 4 \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨(0-(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)),-(0-(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)),(3{sin}^{2}⁡t+3{cos}^{2}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-96957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,2⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,3⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-\\sqrt{t},0,\\sqrt{3-t}⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-\\sqrt{3-t},0,-\\sqrt{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-\\sqrt{t},0,\\sqrt{3-t}⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-\\sqrt{3-t},0,-\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\sqrt{t} & 0 & \\sqrt{3-t} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3-t} & 0 & -\\sqrt{t}\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{3-t} \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{t} & \\sqrt{3-t} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3-t} & -\\sqrt{t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{t} & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3-t} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨0-0,-(t+(3-t)),0-0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,-3,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-127613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨0,-1,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨0,-\\sqrt{3-t},\\sqrt{t}⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{3-t},\\sqrt{t},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,-1,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨0,{e}^{t},1⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨0,1,-{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨0,{e}^{t},1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨0,1,-{e}^{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}+1}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}+1}⟨-{e}^{2t}-1,-(0-0),0-0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}+1}⟨-({e}^{2t}+1),0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}+1}⟨{e}^{2t}+1,1,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨{e}^{t},0,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,-1,2⟩, \\\\ N(2) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-1,2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(2) & =T(2)\\times N(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,-1,2⟩\\times \\frac{1}{3}⟨-1,2,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}⟨(-2-4),-(4+2),(4-1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}⟨-6,-6,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96958" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-96958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2,-2,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}⟨-3,2,\\sqrt{3}⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}⟨-2,4,\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,3⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}⟨-1,-1,4⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96958" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2,-2,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=1,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩, \\\\ N(1) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,-1,2\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(1) & =T(1)\\times N(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩\\times \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,-1,2\\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12}⟨(2\\sqrt{2}-(-\\sqrt{2})),-(-2\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}),(1-3)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12}⟨2\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2},-(-5\\sqrt{2}),-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{12}⟨3\\sqrt{2},5\\sqrt{2},-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{12}⟨3,5,-\\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨3,5,-\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{3}}⟨3,5\\sqrt{2},4⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}⟨3,5,-\\sqrt{2}⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2},-5,3⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}⟨-1,1,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}⟨3,5,-\\sqrt{2}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\times N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨(-15-0),-(-9-16),(0-20)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨-15,25,-20⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}⟨2,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨1,0,3⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩, \\\\ N(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨0,-\\sqrt{3},-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =T(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\times N(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩\\times \\frac{1}{2}⟨0,-\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨(1+3),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨4,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99430" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}⟨4,-1,-2⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,-2,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1,0⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99430" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,0,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=1,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩, \\\\ N(1) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(1) & =T(1)\\times N(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}⟨(-4-5),-(-4-(-4)),(10-(-8))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}⟨-9,0,18⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,1,2⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}⟨3,-4,0⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-1,1,1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99420" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨t,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{2t}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}},\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+{(-2t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{16+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+4)^{3/2}}⟨4,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩}{(\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}+4})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨2,\\,-t,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨t,2,0⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨2,\\,-t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ t & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+4}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}t & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ 2 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+4}⟨0+0,-(0-0),-{t}^{2}-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+4}⟨0,\\,0,\\,-({t}^{2}+4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,1,0⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}⟨0,1,t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨-2,t,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,-1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-0,-(-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}),-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨0,\\,2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{1}{3})}=⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨({sin}^{2}⁡t-(-{cos}^{2}⁡t)),-(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-0),(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-96959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-96959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨1,0,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4t}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{2}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{2}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\sqrt{(-2t)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{2}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,1⟩}{(\\frac{2}{1+4{t}^{2}})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨1,0,2t⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2t \\\\ -2t & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2t \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2t \\\\ -2t & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}⟨0-0,-(1+4{t}^{2}),0-0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}⟨0,\\,-(1+4{t}^{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-127686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+8{t}^{2}}}⟨2t,\\,2t,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2+4{t}^{2}}}⟨-2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-1,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-127686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,-1,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}⟨2{e}^{2t},1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(4{e}^{4t}+1)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{8{e}^{4t}}{(4{e}^{4t}+1)^{3/2}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(4{e}^{4t}+1)^{3/2}}⟨1,\\,-2{e}^{2t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(4{e}^{4t}+1)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+{(-2{e}^{2t})}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(4{e}^{4t}+1)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{4{e}^{4t}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{(4{e}^{4t}+1)^{3/2}}⟨1,-2{e}^{2t},0⟩}{(\\frac{4{e}^{2t}}{4{e}^{4t}+1})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}⟨1,\\,-2{e}^{2t},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}⟨2{e}^{2t},1,0⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{e}^{4t}+1}}⟨1,\\,-2{e}^{2t},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4t}+1}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2{e}^{2t} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4t}+1}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2{e}^{2t} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4t}+1}⟨0+0,-(0-0),-4{e}^{4t}-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4t}+1}⟨0,0,-(4{e}^{4t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b41aa0ef40d98972a76d753c191ada4cef41ace2fd781dcdfad39a84485dee2c"} {"question" "q-99653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,0,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "q-99653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,0,\\,-1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/state.json" "file_sha256" "27564d7071e6eca17381fdae659630a875ea039c20fa50dbc7480ed605db2dbb"} {"question" "e-8595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,t,4⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,4,-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/example-8595.json" "file_sha256" "209705124c51df0a551d396384a2258fa6726d9bfb555e1ebcc026d43d262671"} {"question" "e-8595" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,t,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,4,-t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & t & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ 4 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & t \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}⟨(-{t}^{2}-16),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}⟨-({t}^{2}+16),0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/example-8595.json" "file_sha256" "209705124c51df0a551d396384a2258fa6726d9bfb555e1ebcc026d43d262671"} {"question" "e-8596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t=\\pi$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\pi ) & =⟨1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/example-8596.json" "file_sha256" "abddef178bb66fe484028d452228eb58aab370b014c2a35aff5b5186e580cac5"} {"question" "e-8596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\pi ) & =T(\\pi )\\times N(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3,4⟩\\times ⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨(0-0),-(0-4),(0-(-3))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/example-8596.json" "file_sha256" "abddef178bb66fe484028d452228eb58aab370b014c2a35aff5b5186e580cac5"} {"question" "e-8597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/example-8597.json" "file_sha256" "0ae202263b161a042d0276bec9549fcd2b763d029ef42c822a9067f5d65e772b"} {"question" "e-8597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $\\mathbf N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf N(t)= \\dfrac{\\mathbf T'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $\\mathbf{N}(t).$ To do this, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡4t+16{sin}^{2}⁡4t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡4t+{sin}^{2}⁡4t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩}{(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡4t-{cos}^{2}⁡4t),0-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,1,\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071630/example-8597.json" "file_sha256" "0ae202263b161a042d0276bec9549fcd2b763d029ef42c822a9067f5d65e772b"}] "usage" {"e-8595" [] "q-96958" [] "q-96959" [] "q-99504" [] "e-8596" [] "q-96957" [] "e-8597" []} "basis" 2566 "retractions" [[17592186167434 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$T(t)|= \\frac{1}{5}⟨ - 3\\sin t, 3\\cos t, 4⟩,; N(t)|= ⟨ - \\cos t,-\\sin t, 0⟩$.\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [17592186167435 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t = 2$, given that\n\n$T(2)|= \\frac{1}{3}⟨2,-1, 2⟩,; N(2)|= \\frac{1}{3}⟨ - 1, 2, 2⟩$.\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [17592186167476 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$T(t)|= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 4}}⟨t, 2, 0⟩$.\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector."] [17592186167436 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$T(t)|= \\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\sin t, \\cos t⟩$.\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector."] [17592186166609 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n$T(t)|= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 16}}⟨0, t, 4⟩,; N(t)|= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 16}}⟨0, 4,-t⟩$.\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [17592186166609 :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(t) &= T(t) \\cdot N(t) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 16}}⟨0, t, 4⟩ \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{2} + 16}}⟨0, 4,-t⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{t^{2} + 16}i\\begin{vmatrix}j & k \\\\ 0 & t\\end{vmatrix}4 \\\\\n&= 0 \\mid 4\\begin{vmatrix}-t \\\\ = \\frac{1}{t^{2} + 16}[t\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{vmatrix}- ti - 0\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{vmatrix}- tj + 0 \\mid t \\\\\n&= 0\\end{vmatrix}4k] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{t^{2} + 16}⟨(-t^{2} - 16), - (0 - 0), (0 - 0)⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{t^{2} + 16}⟨ - (t^{2} + 16), 0, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 1, 0, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186166610 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t=\\pi$, given that\n\n$T(π)|= \\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3, 4⟩,; N(π)|= ⟨1, 0, 0⟩$.\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."] [17592186166610 :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(π) &= T(π) \\cdot N(π) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3, 4⟩ \\cdot ⟨1, 0, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}i\\begin{vmatrix}j & k \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}4 \\\\\n&= 1 \\mid 0\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\\\ = \\frac{1}{5}[- 3\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{vmatrix}0i - 0\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{vmatrix}0j + 0 \\mid - 3 \\\\\n&= 1\\end{vmatrix}0k] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}⟨(0 - 0), - (0 - 4), (0 - (-3))⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}⟨0, 4, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186166611 :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$T(t)|= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\sin 4t, 2, \\cos 4t⟩$.\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ denotes the unit tangent vector."] [17592186166611 :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t)\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $\\mathbf N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf N(t)= \\dfrac{\\mathbf T'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $\\mathbf{N}(t)$. To do this, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT^{′}(t) &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sin 4t), \\frac{d}{dt}(2), \\frac{d}{dt}(\\cos 4t)⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨4\\cos 4t, 0,-4\\sin 4t⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩ \\\\\n‖T^{′}(t)‖ &= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(4\\cos 4t)^{2} + 0^{2} + (-4\\sin 4t)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16\\cos^{2} 4t + 16\\sin^{2} 4t} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16(\\cos^{2} 4t + \\sin^{2} 4t)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(t) &= (T^{′}(t))/(‖T^{′}(t)‖) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩)/((\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})) \\\\\n&= ⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(t) &= T(t) \\cdot N(t) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\sin 4t, 2, \\cos 4t⟩ \\cdot ⟨\\cos 4t, 0,-\\sin 4t⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}i\\begin{vmatrix}j & k \\\\ \\sin 4t & 2\\end{vmatrix}\\cos 4t \\\\\n&= \\cos 4t \\mid 0\\begin{vmatrix}-\\sin 4t \\\\ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[2\\begin{vmatrix}\\cos 4t \\\\ 0\\end{vmatrix}- \\sin 4ti - \\sin 4t\\begin{vmatrix}\\cos 4t \\\\ \\cos 4t\\end{vmatrix}- \\sin 4tj + \\sin 4t \\mid 2 \\\\\n&= \\cos 4t\\end{vmatrix}0k] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨ - 2\\sin 4t - 0, - (-\\sin^{2} 4t - \\cos^{2} 4t), 0 - 2\\cos 4t⟩ \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨ - 2\\sin 4t, 1,-2\\cos 4t⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186166153 17592186166154 17592186166155 17592186166156 17592186166157 17592186166159 17592186166160 17592186166161 17592186166162 17592186166163 17592186166165 17592186166166 17592186166167 17592186166168 17592186166169 17592186166405 17592186166406 17592186166407 17592186166408 17592186166409] "immutable_fields" [[17592186166152 :answer-field/correct] [17592186166152 :answer-field/id] [17592186166152 :answer-field/key] [17592186166152 :answer-field/type] [17592186166158 :answer-field/correct] [17592186166158 :answer-field/id] [17592186166158 :answer-field/key] [17592186166158 :answer-field/type] [17592186166164 :answer-field/correct] [17592186166164 :answer-field/id] [17592186166164 :answer-field/key] [17592186166164 :answer-field/type] [17592186166404 :answer-field/correct] [17592186166404 :answer-field/id] [17592186166404 :answer-field/key] [17592186166404 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
